create the app non-interactively by automating the GitHub manifest UI (headless
Playwright) or by using a provided --code, exchange the returned temporary code
for the created app credentials and write them to the corresponding .env.prod file.

This script supports:
 - Fully non-interactive headless creation via --headless (requires playwright)
 - TOTP-based 2FA automation via GITHUB_2FA_TOTP (pyotp)
 - Non-interactive direct exchange if you already have the temporary --code
 - Optional upload of secrets to a GitHub repository's Actions secrets using
   --github-repo (requires GITHUB_TOKEN with repo scope) and PyNaCl.

Dependencies (install into your environment):
  pip install requests python-dotenv PyNaCl pyotp playwright
  # then install browsers for playwright:
  playwright install

Usage examples:
  # Headless create both apps using TRAEFIK_DOMAIN env var:
  python scripts/create_github_app_manifests.py --all --headless

  # Headless create one app, write secrets to repo owner/repo
  export GITHUB_TOKEN="ghp_..."  # must have repo permissions
  export GITHUB_LOGIN=""
  export GITHUB_PASSWORD=""
  export GITHUB_2FA_TOTP="BASE32_TOTP_SECRET"  # optional, if account uses TOTP 2FA
  python-scripts:(".create/github/app/manifests.py")--app github-app-node --headless --github-repo owner/repo

  # Non-interactive when you already have the temporary code:
  python scripts/create_github_app_manifests.py --app github-app-node --code abcd1234

Notes:
 - Automating browser sign-in is inherently brittle (GitHub may change the UI).
 - Using credentials in CI has security implications; prefer machine accounts
   with least privilege.
"""
